# What gets uploaded to Vercel.
#
# `public/` is the built site (~736 MB) and `api/` holds the serverless
# functions. The capture sources are excluded: they are another ~736 MB, they
# are not needed to serve anything, and the 515 MB of pre-rebrand backups in
# _quarantine/ must never leave this machine.
#
# `package.json` has to be uploaded or Vercel cannot install the two runtime
# dependencies the API needs (@neondatabase/serverless, resend). It deliberately
# has no `build` script — if it did, Vercel would run it and fail, because the
# sources `build:vercel` copies from are not uploaded.
#
# `/*` ignores top-level entries only, so the un-ignored directories below are
# still descended into. Ignoring a directory outright would stop Vercel from
# ever looking inside it, and no `!` rule could bring its contents back.

/*

!/public
!/api
!/vercel.json
!/package.json
!/package-lock.json
